</node>
<node id="&quot;GOVERNMENTAL AUTHORITY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"REGULATORY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A governmental authority is a regulatory body that has the power to enforce laws and regulations."&lt;SEP&gt;"A regulatory authority responsible for overseeing and enforcing compliance with laws, rules, and regulations that govern credit agreements and financial transactions."&lt;SEP&gt;"An authority that has the power to regulate and oversee financial markets."&lt;SEP&gt;"Any Governmental Authority charged with the enforcement, interpretation or administration of Laws."&lt;SEP&gt;"Any government agency or authority that has the power to regulate or oversee financial transactions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Any government or regulatory body that has authority over the Company or the credit agreement."&lt;SEP&gt;"Refers to the authorities or bodies responsible for overseeing and enforcing compliance with laws, rules, and regulations that govern credit agreements and financial transactions."&lt;SEP&gt;"The authorities or bodies responsible for overseeing and enforcing compliance with laws, rules, and regulations that govern credit agreements and financial transactions."&lt;SEP&gt;"or if any Borrower is required to pay any Indemnified Taxes or additional amounts to any Lender or any Governmental Authority for the account of any Lender pursuant to Section 3.01"&lt;SEP&gt;"the authority responsible for overseeing and enforcing compliance with laws and regulations."&lt;SEP&gt;"the government of the United States or any other nation, or of any political subdivision thereof, whether state or local, and any agency, authority, instrumentality, regulatory body, court, central bank or other entity exercising executive, legislative, judicial, taxing, regulatory or administrative powers or functions of or pertaining to government."&lt;SEP&gt;"to secure partial, progress, advance or other payments pursuant to any contract or statute or to secure any Indebtedness incurred for the purpose of financing all or any part of the purchase price or the cost of constructing or improving property or assets subject to such Liens"&lt;SEP&gt;"to the relevant Governmental Authority in accordance with the Code, and (C) to the extent that the withholding or deduction is made on account of Indemnified Taxes, the sum payable by the applicable Borrower shall be increased as necessary so that after any required withholding or the making of all required deductions (including deductions applicable to additional sums payable under this Section) the applicable Recipient receives an amount equal to the sum it would have received had no such withholding or deduction been made."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3d5eca3d410c6e7af1c12511c011937aecc77644104b8212bfaf1761e84d991a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cc3aeda4c8edfd097445eb549ccb4a90e255e5a840b3e4e803abe3a81e80fda1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b285e03d7146f17e87848eb9b5f8c15183dec4084105eaa7e79c1ad84c91367&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-be25a46cca3a79843b2c8a4c855abca0c524be4f23bd13985d7ed013c2da3408&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c5e48532ee920b5375a652dc8e8d0fdfd2761dd7785efd024ee1ed1feb0d9303&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4a9c6ebe9b09f0c3d719105cd8ced9a6a8b5cdc9b6070153b8c9d8082f94c0d7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d284a32dc973551dd3a95e067c7a7e4ca65ed5fc4b8b9af49298c1a4ab4c8738&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7b382365636e7d7745a443218cd6b4521b203ff098b36b45bf2b0ac9d851d876&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-652de4f4d91e90a6f7563949dee043c59ebc83c69af5a7e4daaf8634d33d43cd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ffa333ba0635dfede67f8ea5e9914c4783139c8fc1ab497336bf6f481fabdc91&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5d34bfe4b8431df4ba4815a275fd36ac0a378cd81d05748dd022697a48707a14&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4a34ec7ffc5432911519463a4d806edde9566d8d3383aef9f37db8ac12227f88&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e7176cf30b46b0b2bd028f692a631973b82ef94973df4a23df2be2494830423d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ff14b04e79a66fbfb8528158967e7f8c27d18cd00c1753f7623ec5b24aeafbe6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9bd758a235fa3762ad9b4aad4608ccd04d2283533e76b28c157982eac1454264</data>
  <data key="d3">DOC-5619df3ed8174d0d8a59a7c69c0d2e4d08b31bfa20e08b964330e5d3d2b5c6eb</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FIVE-YEAR REVOLVING CREDIT AGREEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"AGREEMENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A credit agreement outlining the terms of the loan, including the lender, borrower, and repayment terms."&lt;SEP&gt;"A legally binding contract outlining the terms of the loan, including the rights and obligations of the parties involved."&lt;SEP&gt;"FIVE-YEAR REVOLVING CREDIT AGREEMENT dated as of November 1, 2023"&lt;SEP&gt;"The FIVE-YEAR REVOLVING CREDIT AGREEMENT is the contract outlining the terms of the loan between CITIBANK, N.A. and AMAZON.COM, INC.."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Five-Year Revolving Credit Agreement is a contract between AMAZON.COM, INC. and the lender, outlining the terms of the loan."&lt;SEP&gt;"The agreement is a five-year revolving credit facility provided to Amazon.com, Inc. by Deutsche Bank AG New York Branch."&lt;SEP&gt;"The agreement is a legally binding contract outlining the terms of the loan, including the rights and obligations of the parties involved."&lt;SEP&gt;"The agreement is a legally binding contract outlining the terms of the loan."&lt;SEP&gt;"The contract outlining the terms and conditions of the revolving credit facility provided by Bank of America N.A. to Amazon.com, Inc."&lt;SEP&gt;"The contract outlining the terms of the credit arrangement between Amazon.com, Inc. and Barclays Bank PLC."&lt;SEP&gt;"The credit agreement between Amazon.com, Inc. and Bank of China, Los Angeles Branch."&lt;SEP&gt;"The credit agreement between Amazon.com, Inc. and HSBC Bank USA, National Association."&lt;SEP&gt;"The credit agreement between Amazon.com, Inc. and JPMorgan Chase Bank, N.A."&lt;SEP&gt;"The credit agreement between Amazon.com, Inc. and Royal Bank of Canada."&lt;SEP&gt;"The credit agreement between Amazon.com, Inc. and Societe Generale."&lt;SEP&gt;"The credit agreement between Amazon.com, Inc. and Standard Chartered Bank."&lt;SEP&gt;"The credit agreement between Amazon.com, Inc. and The Bank of Nova Scotia."&lt;SEP&gt;"The credit agreement between Amazon.com, Inc. and The Hongkong and Shanghai Bank Corporation Limited."&lt;SEP&gt;"The credit agreement between Amazon.com, Inc. and U.S. Bank National Association."&lt;SEP&gt;"The credit agreement between Amazon.com, Inc. and Wells Fargo Bank, N.A."&lt;SEP&gt;"The formal contract outlining the terms of the credit arrangement between Amazon.com, Inc. and Banco Bilbao Vizcaya Argentaria, S.A."&lt;SEP&gt;"The specific credit agreement between Amazon.com, Inc. and BNP Paribas."&lt;SEP&gt;"The type of credit agreement between Amazon.com, Inc. and The Toronto-Dominion Bank, New York Branch."</data>
