  <data key="d1">"Indebtedness refers to the amount borrowed by the Company or its Subsidiaries, and the agreement outlines various types of indebtedness that may be secured by liens."&lt;SEP&gt;"Indebtedness refers to the borrower's obligations under the credit agreement."&lt;SEP&gt;"The amount of debt owed by the borrower to the lender."&lt;SEP&gt;"all of the following, whether or not included as indebtedness or liabilities in accordance with GAAP: obligations for borrowed money, obligations evidenced by bonds, debentures, notes, loan agreements or other similar instruments, direct or contingent obligations arising under letters of credit, and net obligations under any Swap Contract."&lt;SEP&gt;"any Indebtedness incurred by the Company or any Subsidiary for the purpose of financing all or any part of the purchase price of any property or assets"</data>
