  <data key="d0">"COVENANTS"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A clause in the credit agreement that outlines the terms and conditions for indemnified taxes or additional amounts."&lt;SEP&gt;"A specific part of the credit agreement that outlines terms and conditions related to taxes and indemnifications."&lt;SEP&gt;"A specific section of the credit agreement that outlines the terms and conditions for taxes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Specific promises or restrictions included in the agreement that govern the borrower's operations and financial behavior."&lt;SEP&gt;"all of its interests, rights (other than its existing rights to payments pursuant to Sections 3.01 and 3.04) and obligations under this Agreement and the related Loan Documents to an Eligible Assignee that shall assume such obligations."&lt;SEP&gt;"or if any Borrower is required to pay any Indemnified Taxes or additional amounts to any Lender or any Governmental Authority for the account of any Lender pursuant to Section 3.01"&lt;SEP&gt;"such Lender shall cease to be a party hereto but shall continue to be entitled to the benefits of Sections 3.01, 3.04, 3.05, and 11.04 with respect to facts and circumstances occurring prior to the effective date of such assignment."&lt;SEP&gt;"the section of the agreement that specifies the requirements for withholding Taxes."</data>
