<node id="&quot;MATERIAL ADVERSE EFFECT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"DEFAULT INTEREST"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A higher interest rate applied when the borrower fails to meet payment obligations, serving as a penalty and an incentive to maintain timely payments."&lt;SEP&gt;"A material adverse change in, or a material adverse effect upon, the financial condition of the Company and its Subsidiaries, taken as a whole."&lt;SEP&gt;"A material adverse effect is an event that has a significant impact on the company's financial condition."&lt;SEP&gt;"unless such Taxes are being contested in good faith by appropriate proceedings diligently conducted, or would not reasonably be expected to result in a Material Adverse Effect."</data>
