<node id="&quot;ADMINISTRATIVE AGENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"AGENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">The Administrative Agent is a designated entity, often a bank or financial intermediary, tasked with managing the administrative and operational aspects of the credit agreement. This includes fund disbursement, communication, and coordination among participants, such as lenders and borrowers. The Administrative Agent is appointed by the lenders to act on their behalf and manage the loan documents and transactions contemplated in the credit agreement. 

The Administrative Agent is responsible for determining certain rates and benchmarks, such as the Overnight Rate and the Benchmark Replacement, in accordance with banking industry rules and the credit agreement. The Administrative Agent also maintains the confidentiality of information and is authorized to set off and apply any deposits or obligations against the obligations of the company or any other borrower.

In the event of a default or other issue, the Administrative Agent may take certain actions, such as notifying the lenders and borrowers, determining the US Dollar Equivalent of any loan denominated in an Alternative Currency, and making deductions or withholdings as necessary. The Administrative Agent may also modify certain definitions, such as the definition of "Interest Period," to remove unavailable or non-representative tenors.

The Administrative Agent has the same rights and powers as any other lender and may exercise these rights as though it were not the Administrative Agent. The entity serving as the Administrative Agent may be removed and replaced by the Required Lenders if it becomes a Defaulting Lender.

Examples of entities acting as Administrative Agents include CITIBANK, N.A. and JPMorgan Chase Bank, N.A. The Administrative Agent's books and records are admissible in evidence in any action or proceeding and are binding upon the company. The company may designate additional subsidiaries as Designated Borrowers, and the Administrative Agent shall maintain a copy of each Assignment and Assumption delivered to it. 

Overall, the Administrative Agent plays a crucial role in managing the administrative and operational aspects of the credit agreement, ensuring that the terms and conditions of the agreement are met, and that the rights and obligations of the lenders and borrowers are protected.</data>
