<node id="&quot;LENDER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LENDER"</data>
  <data key="d1">The LENDER is a financial institution or entity that provides loans to borrowers under a credit agreement. As a lender, it is responsible for disbursing funds and monitoring compliance with the credit agreement. The LENDER has the right to bring actions, litigation, or proceedings against the company or designated borrowers. It is also entitled to receive interest on the loans provided, although if the interest exceeds the Maximum Rate, the excess interest shall be applied to the principal of the loans or refunded to the company. 

The LENDER's commitment to make loans to the borrowers is outlined in the credit agreement, and it may sell participations to any person without the consent of or notice to any borrower or the administrative agent. If a LENDER fails to fund all or any portion of its loans within two business days of the date such loans were required to be funded, it may be considered a Defaulting Lender. 

Examples of LENDERS include Banco Santander, S.A., New York Branch, Deutsche Bank AG New York Branch, JPMorgan Chase Bank, N.A., and Wells Fargo Bank, N.A. These financial institutions provide financing to companies, such as AMAZON.COM, INC., under credit agreements, including five-year revolving credit agreements. The LENDER's role is crucial in providing credit to borrowers and ensuring that the terms of the credit agreement are complied with. 

In the event of a dispute or default, the LENDER may require the company to assign and delegate its rights, and it may also declare the commitment of each LENDER to be terminated. The LENDER is also entitled to rely on notices, requests, certificates, and other documents believed to be genuine and authenticated by the proper person. Overall, the LENDER plays a vital role in providing credit to borrowers and ensuring that the terms of the credit agreement are enforced.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7f9271415b6fffe0893502dc89e3841c2be9f06f82c8c5f9489abaefaec90483&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b285e03d7146f17e87848eb9b5f8c15183dec4084105eaa7e79c1ad84c91367&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-25153dfc8542779016754e3a9d4ba1ff761fe00f9d01723cf4b526a3637e8e65&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a26b5126e4c1e707b1bbe422f1a41e0d0cc8063a093ce84f380bccb1d3545594&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c7db0278db53932718c0ec9229e65778e4ed2f8d1c18cc7df9db844e9044f91d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c5e48532ee920b5375a652dc8e8d0fdfd2761dd7785efd024ee1ed1feb0d9303&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-405e30a8247fa3f574e4cf704c4da2490c7b07557815fff2ebf7de66149d000a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-21e8bd401eb8d2893cda3131348d5d8ecee9345959902e114ca131d8e2d1d670&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eeefb9b088abc8d89a40d93af5939ed01899b461f9a1e8dbd62765acc3ca0f5c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e425af2e275bc52ded23404cc180bda000dd6a0c5f29625d84cb283b1e6497a6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e56521f0d5861a7f4d9b333237148742c844e3d8c2104929a676973533b40aca&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a05f2d3762035b6920e2994449915a10f14de2b16d9908fab1975c1279ab5fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2f3af823220981638c48fc83a90df748a59607384581d6688401c7c9cd5c1fd7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dfab8e567e4b2e5380b905a1150a53c7223642e58e7a7f29499f7f19b9bed867&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c4c601fe8f9d4d8b25c08bf113b5bf96ae2574679bd1e9086048018d2759a602&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-63858fdc1fc34af26e481d6c4df137e48430e981c53ec2578449a748506facd2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7b2e35c49fdc82fe469355cd3f4a7d66ac4e1caf86823c8a1f714e6758a00f72&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c4a164963b51c81b4b7d5b333e9db2c3903e435b22d1b0a8d407e7203d895bb0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-48de9c0c4ee7fbda3257454472e1f74bc0487f3f3bb847feab2a439c61845295&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9cf30aa371483ffc5e424225ef332db8adf37eeb6519c28e0905154c67a5e75e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-26e39a9e3ce38e35ba80037cbf39058662ce1dbd88dd87d6a9a695b35bb692f1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4b0b12585f6502351b0e84ecc60e47e6640828e4339d67c9b7a3c5084dcdb713&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cc3aeda4c8edfd097445eb549ccb4a90e255e5a840b3e4e803abe3a81e80fda1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0e8dd65b0bdcd2760aee8bbedd800f7746b7142b5f61618f2af7cedb31ba6ce9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-be25a46cca3a79843b2c8a4c855abca0c