<edge source="&quot;BORROWER&quot;" target="&quot;LENDER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">478.0</data>
  <data key="d5">The Borrower and the Lender are parties to a credit agreement where the Lender provides a loan to the Borrower, with the expectation of repayment. The Borrower receives funds from the Lender, either directly or through an Administrative Agent, and is responsible for repaying the loan according to the agreed terms, including any interest and fees. The Lender monitors compliance with the credit agreement and may engage in business with the Borrower. In the event that the Borrower requests a loan in a currency other than US Dollars, the Lender has the discretion to consent or refuse. The Borrower is also required to execute and deliver a Note to the assignee Lender upon request. The Lender's role includes providing financing to the Borrower, making loans available, and overseeing the repayment process. The Administrative Agent plays a key role in facilitating the loan process, with the Lender making the loan amount available to the Administrative Agent, who then makes the funds available to the Borrower. Overall, the relationship between the Borrower and the Lender is based on the Lender providing credit to the Borrower under the Credit Agreement, with the Borrower being obligated to repay the loan as agreed upon.</data>
