</edge>
<edge source="&quot;BORROWER&quot;" target="&quot;ADMINISTRATIVE AGENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">285.0</data>
  <data key="d5">The Administrative Agent and the Borrower are two entities involved in a credit agreement. The Administrative Agent acts on behalf of the Lenders to manage the credit agreement, and the Borrower is responsible for repaying the loan. The Administrative Agent administers the credit agreement, determines the US Dollar Equivalent of any Loan denominated in an Alternative Currency for the Borrower, and has the authority to enforce rights and remedies against the Borrower. The Administrative Agent also manages the Loan and distributes payments to the Lenders on behalf of the Borrower. 

The Borrower interacts with the Administrative Agent for matters related to the loan, including fund disbursement, communication, coordination, tax refunds, and indemnifications. The Borrower is required to comply with the terms of the credit agreement, which is managed by the Administrative Agent, and to deliver evidence of payments to the Administrative Agent. The Borrower must pay any amount of principal of any Loan or interest on any Loan to the Administrative Agent, who is responsible for managing the administrative and operational aspects of the credit agreement.

In addition, the Administrative Agent has the authority to make deductions or withholdings and to reimburse itself for any payments made to Governmental Authorities on behalf of the Borrower. The Administrative Agent also gives prompt notice to the Lenders of any requests made by the Borrower and determines whether the requested Interest Period is acceptable to all of them. The Administrative Agent may take actions at the request of, or with the consent of, the Required Lenders, and makes all funds received available to the applicable Borrower. 

Furthermore, Such Person and its Affiliates may engage in business with the Borrower or any Subsidiary or other Affiliate thereof, including accepting deposits, lending money, owning securities, and acting as a financial advisor. Overall, the Administrative Agent plays a crucial role in managing the credit agreement and facilitating the relationship between the Borrower and the Lenders, while the Borrower is responsible for repaying the loan and complying with the terms of the credit agreement.</data>
