</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ADMINISTRATIVE AGENT&quot;" target="&quot;COMPANY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">415.0</data>
  <data key="d5">The Administrative Agent and the Company have a complex relationship where the Administrative Agent acts as an intermediary between the Company and the Lenders, managing the administrative and operational aspects of the credit agreement on behalf of the Company. The Administrative Agent is responsible for communicating with the Company regarding the credit agreement, administering the credit agreement, and determining the Benchmark Replacement. The Company makes payments to the Lenders through the Administrative Agent and is required to deliver financial statements to the Administrative Agent. The Administrative Agent is also authorized to set off and apply any deposits or obligations against the obligations of the Company or any other Borrower.

The Company has appointed the Administrative Agent to manage the administrative and operational aspects of the credit agreement, including fund disbursement and communication among participants. The Company interacts with the Administrative Agent to fulfill their obligations under the credit agreement and pays fees to the Administrative Agent on or before the Closing Date. The Company may at any time, upon notice to the Administrative Agent, designate any additional Subsidiary of the Company as a Designated Borrower or terminate the Aggregate Commitments.

The Administrative Agent delivers written notice of determination to the Company, which is responsible for receiving such notice. The Administrative Agent shall be deemed not to have knowledge of any Default unless and until notice is given in writing to the Administrative Agent by the Company or a Lender. The Administrative Agent shall notify the Company of each Lender's determination under this Section promptly after the Response Date. The Administrative Agent will have the right to make, with the consent of the Company, Benchmark Replacement Conforming Changes from time to time.

The Company has designated the Administrative Agent as its agent to receive, accept, and acknowledge service of process on its behalf. The motivations of the Administrative Agent are commercial in nature and not to invest in the general performance or operations of the Company or any Subsidiary. The Company shall pay all reasonable and documented out-of-pocket expenses incurred by the Administrative Agent and its Affiliates in connection with the syndication of the credit facility provided for herein. Overall, the Administrative Agent plays a crucial role in managing the credit agreement and facilitating communication between the Company and the Lenders.</data>
