<edge source="&quot;ADMINISTRATIVE AGENT&quot;" target="&quot;LENDER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">677.0</data>
  <data key="d5">The Administrative Agent and the Lender have a complex relationship in managing the credit agreement. The Administrative Agent acts on behalf of the Lender in managing the loan, handling administrative and operational aspects, including communication, coordination, and fund disbursement. The Lender appoints the Administrative Agent to manage these aspects and has a funding obligation to the Administrative Agent, which is responsible for delivering written notice of determination to each borrower and each lender. The Administrative Agent is also responsible for notifying the Lender of any errors and managing the administrative aspects of the credit agreement, including taxes and refunds.

The Lender is required to deliver tax documentation to the Administrative Agent, who determines whether the Lender is subject to backup withholding or information reporting requirements. The Lender must also indemnify the Administrative Agent against any Indemnified Taxes attributable to the Lender. The Administrative Agent and the Lender work together in connection with the enforcement or protection of their rights under the agreement and other loan documents.

In terms of loan management, the Administrative Agent manages the Lender's interests and obligations under the credit agreement, including handling taxes and refunds. The Administrative Agent also coordinates payments and distributes funds on behalf of the Lenders. The Lender notifies the Administrative Agent of their consent to making loans in a requested currency, and the Administrative Agent notifies each Lender of any request for an additional currency.

The Administrative Agent has the same rights and powers as any other Lender and may exercise these rights as though it were not the Administrative Agent. The Administrative Agent is entitled to rely on notices, requests, certificates, and other documents believed to be genuine and authenticated by the proper person. The Lender agrees to return any erroneous payment to the Administrative Agent, who is responsible for notifying the Lender of any errors.

The Administrative Agent and the Lender have a relationship where the Administrative Agent manages the administrative and operational aspects of the credit agreement on behalf of the Lender. The Lender makes representations and warranties to the Administrative Agent regarding their use of plan assets in connection with the loans or commitments. The Administrative Agent records the assignments and assumptions of the Lenders in the register and is responsible for managing the administrative aspects of the credit agreement.

Overall, the Administrative Agent plays a crucial role in managing the credit agreement on behalf of the Lender, handling administrative and operational aspects, and coordinating payments and distributions. The Lender has a funding obligation to the Administrative Agent and must indemnify the Administrative Agent against any Indemnified Taxes attributable to the Lender. The Administrative Agent and the Lender work together</data>
